NOTE = '''0.3.32 (2026-10-17) = THE APPROVED ABILITY ICONS ON THE ABILITIES WIDGET, EVERY CLASS (RESUME small list "Hud ability icons (6 classes)";
docs/log 2026-10-16 "PINNED emblems ... Hud ability widget icons for 6 classes = later Hud round"; Skyy 2026-10-17: "work through your whole
todo list ... pich what fits the existing build."). 0.3.18-0.3.31 shipped their OWN copies of the 10 Mage + Priest pictures
(Common/UI/Custom/SkyyHud/Abil/<Id>.png, a Group Background) and showed nothing for Monk, Assassin, Warrior, Berserker, Archer, Spellblade.
  1. ONE PICTURE, OWNED BY SKYYCLASSES: each row's icon is now an ItemIcon of the ability's icon item id - the id SkyyClasses 0.1.36+ sends in
     class:fn:abilPanel o[12 + 16 i + 2] (AbilDefs.ICON: the hidden rune item SkyyAbility_<Class>_<Id> wearing the approved art/ability-icons
     picture, Guardian Spirit = SkyyClasses_Icon_GuardianSpirit; "" when that item is not loaded) - the same ids and the same ItemIcon way
     SkyyTrees' nodes / Lattice, SkyyWardrobe's ability slots and SkyyClasses' own /cast page show. So all 8 classes (40 approved pictures;
     Challenge + Guardian's Oath wear the stand-ins SkyyClasses gives them everywhere) and every later icon come with SkyyClasses, nothing
     to copy. The 10 own PNG copies + ABL_ICON_IDS / AICONS / ADIR / abilIcon are GONE from SkyyHud (no duplicate pictures).
  2. Matching: the icon is used only while the abilPanel slot id equals the class:fn:abil slot id of that row (the 0.3.24 level rule) and
     the id is letters / digits / _ only; otherwise the row shows its name only (as with Icons Hide). abilPanel is still asked at most once
     per player per 5 s (the 0.3.24 cache), so after a loadout swap the new icon follows within 5 s. abilLvOf now also keeps the slot ids
     + icons when ability levels are off (levels still need [8] true + a level above 0, exactly as before).
  3. DIMMED: while the row cools down (its bar shows) or is grey (cannot pay Mana / Stamina, locked "Lv 10", Soon), the vanilla sold-out
     cover (kit cardOverlay #0a0e12(0.75), BarterTradeRow #OutOfStockOverlay) lies over the icon (#<base>D<k>); ready rows show it plain.
     The shape string already carries bar / grey / icon, so a state change re-sends the widget exactly as before - no new update path.
  4. The editor / Settings sample shows SkyyAbility_Mage_Meteor (ready) + SkyyAbility_Mage_ManaBarrier (cooling down = dimmed) while
     SkyyClasses 0.1.36+ is loaded (class:fn:emblem present) and Icons is Show; it also fixes the 0.3.24 sample line whose comment swallowed
     "m[4] = null; m[5] = "n"; m[6] = ..." (the sample never drew its icon).
  5. ICONS SHOW BY DEFAULT (main session 2026-10-17, Skyy's standing rule, memory "no dev gates": nothing switched off during dev,
     finished features default ON). The old flag cannot tell "never touched" from "chose Hide" (WLayout.opt true = both; a default line
     does not even write it), so the choice gets its OWN value: field 11 "2" = "chose Hide in 0.3.32+" (new WLayout.optH). Every older
     saved value counts as never chosen -> Show: "1" / no field (the old default Hide, or an old explicit Hide - a no-op choice: Hide WAS
     the default and only the 10 Mage + Priest pictures existed, never seen in game) and "0" (the old explicit Show). Abilities Settings:
     Show = optH false (field 11 "0" as before), Hide = optH true (opt true + "2"); the buttons light from optH. Other widgets never set
     optH (their opt is unchanged). Every path that stores a layout goes through WLayout.ser / parse (the player file, layout profiles,
     export codes, the server default layout), so all carry it. A rollback to 0.3.31 reads "2" as opt true = its Hide default.
     Widgets.optOf(id, l) = the option the models get: for Abilities "icons shown" (!optH), else l.opt as before; model() / sampleU()
     pass it straight to abilModelU / abilSample (was !opt).
  Unchanged: the 18 px icon column, every size / width, names, costs, bars, commands, permissions, files, bridge keys. Item pictures inside
  a HUD stay UNVERIFIED until Skyy has looked. Needs nothing new from SkyyClasses (0.1.36+). ROLLBACK to 0.3.31: safe (see 5).
'''

